<figure class="spool-diagram">
	<svg
		viewBox="0 0 960 270"
		role="img"
		aria-label="Two crawlers read issues and documents from Linear and store them in the inbox. The ingester writes them to the bronze layer of the data lake. The mounter turns them into Markdown, splits them into chunks, asks an embedding model for their vectors and writes the chunks to Qdrant as the gold layer, with the source metadata in each payload. The assistant, outside Spool, searches Qdrant and answers with the sources."
	>
		<defs>
			<marker id="kb-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path class="arrowhead" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<rect class="boundary" x="132" y="12" width="708" height="246" rx="10" />
		<text class="boundary-label" x="146" y="32">Spool</text>

		<rect class="external" x="10" y="44" width="100" height="56" rx="6" />
		<text class="name" x="60" y="77" text-anchor="middle">Linear</text>

		<rect class="box" x="150" y="44" width="130" height="56" rx="6" />
		<text class="name" x="215" y="68" text-anchor="middle">crawlers</text>
		<text class="small" x="215" y="88" text-anchor="middle">issues, documents</text>

		<rect class="box" x="330" y="44" width="110" height="56" rx="6" />
		<text class="name" x="385" y="77" text-anchor="middle">ingester</text>

		<rect class="box" x="490" y="44" width="180" height="56" rx="6" />
		<text class="name" x="580" y="68" text-anchor="middle">mounter</text>
		<text class="small" x="580" y="88" text-anchor="middle">Markdown, chunks</text>

		<rect class="store" x="710" y="44" width="116" height="56" rx="4" />
		<text class="name" x="768" y="68" text-anchor="middle">Qdrant</text>
		<text class="small" x="768" y="88" text-anchor="middle">gold layer</text>

		<rect class="external" x="860" y="44" width="92" height="56" rx="6" />
		<text class="name" x="906" y="77" text-anchor="middle">assistant</text>

		<rect class="store" x="230" y="176" width="110" height="50" rx="4" />
		<text class="name" x="285" y="206" text-anchor="middle">inbox</text>

		<rect class="store" x="390" y="176" width="130" height="50" rx="4" />
		<text class="name" x="455" y="198" text-anchor="middle">data lake</text>
		<text class="small" x="455" y="216" text-anchor="middle">bronze layer</text>

		<rect class="external" x="570" y="176" width="170" height="50" rx="6" />
		<text class="name" x="655" y="206" text-anchor="middle">embedding model</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="110" y1="72" x2="147" y2="72" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="70" y="124" text-anchor="middle">polled</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="240" y1="100" x2="268" y2="173" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<line class="edge" x1="305" y1="176" x2="355" y2="103" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="296" y="136" text-anchor="middle">envelopes</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="410" y1="100" x2="440" y2="173" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<line class="edge" x1="480" y1="176" x2="530" y2="103" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="462" y="136" text-anchor="middle">records</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="640" y1="103" x2="640" y2="173" marker-start="url(#kb-arrow)" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="648" y="142">vectors</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="670" y1="72" x2="707" y2="72" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />

		<text class="small" x="768" y="124" text-anchor="middle">each point keeps</text>
		<text class="small" x="768" y="142" text-anchor="middle">correlation id,</text>
		<text class="small" x="768" y="160" text-anchor="middle">source, URL, title</text>

		<line class="edge" x1="857" y1="72" x2="829" y2="72" marker-end="url(#kb-arrow)" />
		<text class="small" x="906" y="124" text-anchor="middle">searches</text>
		<text class="small" x="906" y="142" text-anchor="middle">and cites</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		Everything inside the dashed line runs in Spool, from reading Linear to storing the chunks in Qdrant. Each chunk keeps the metadata of the record it comes from, so the assistant can name the issue or document behind every answer.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
